I try to help people when they need it. I have worked in a few different fields that help people. 

I have worked in a hospital for 15 years as a nurse and I have worked with kids with autism and special needs.

I also volunteer for the American Red Cross and the American Heart Association. &amp;#x200B;

I think it's a bit misleading to say "helping others is an important life goal." I think it's more important to help people who are suffering. It's not helpful to give money to a beggar on the street or help someone with their groceries. It's much better to help a person who is struggling financially.

&amp;#x200B;

